    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0457" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/590</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spring Rice</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 8.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I did not fail to
                    telegraph to Sir E. Grey in the sense of your letter of the 5th relative to
                    rosin. As you are aware, cargoes of rosin shipped prior to the declaration that
                    rosin was contraband (with a reasonable delay), although they may be seized, can
                    not be confiscated but must be paid for, if seized, in full.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
